{"type":"standard","title":"Ralph Alvarado","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ralph Alvarado</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q19519302","titles":{"canonical":"Ralph_Alvarado","normalized":"Ralph Alvarado","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ralph Alvarado</span></span>"},"pageid":45559107,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Ralph_Alvarado_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/330px-Ralph_Alvarado_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":486},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Ralph_Alvarado_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1984,"height":2920},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376721368","tid":"26728476-b92a-11f1-a9a6-af3dae2cdc0b","timestamp":"2026-09-25T21:43:31Z","description":"American physician and politician","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Alvarado","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Alvarado?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Alvarado?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ralph_Alvarado"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Alvarado","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ralph_Alvarado","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Alvarado?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ralph_Alvarado"}},"extract":"Ralph A. Alvarado is an American physician and politician who most recently served as the 15th Commissioner of the Tennessee Department of Health from 2023 until his resignation in 2025. He previously served as a member of the Kentucky Senate, representing Kentucky's 28th Senate district from 2015 to 2023. Upon taking office, he became the first Hispanic person elected to the Kentucky General Assembly.","extract_html":"<p><b>Ralph A. Alvarado</b> is an American physician and politician who most recently served as the 15th Commissioner of the Tennessee Department of Health from 2023 until his resignation in 2025. He previously served as a member of the Kentucky Senate, representing Kentucky's 28th Senate district from 2015 to 2023. Upon taking office, he became the first Hispanic person elected to the Kentucky General Assembly.</p>"}